Settings is now a page beside the door, not a button on top of it: swipe left to reach it, right to come back, and two dots say which one you are on. The door keeps every pixel it had. Settings is a proper list now, so it scrolls, including with the crown, which did nothing anywhere in the app before. It also says which account is signed in, which nothing on the watch did before. And the mic beside the door starts listening the moment it opens, instead of asking for a second tap first.
